/-!
# Ordinary rank-one and higher-field exclusions

The literal rank-one and higher-field constructors of 15.1.20 are excluded
under the original pre-exclusion hypotheses. All linear, unitary, Suzuki
and higher-field models are covered, including the central two-covers.
The actual prime actor handles the exceptional L₂(4) row. In the unitary
row, relative normality and the fixed-field torus supply two-perfectness,
Thompson normalization and the exact Sylow centralizer comparison.

The constructor-aware quotient adapter now needs only the initial
15.1.20 catalogue, and the exchanged-source application retains the same
pre-exclusion witness. That initial classification is not proved here;
its producer belongs to qt-e-15122-ordinary-pre-exclusion, and its discharge
in the early quotient assembly remains with qt-e-15121-ordinary-rankone.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith 15.1.21, printed pp.1097--1098.
-/
